  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "5.1.0\n\nBREAKING: patterns are now validated against the BulletML DTD rules, so some patterns that loaded in 5.0 will throw from ParseXML. Errors are InvalidDataException, wrapped in an exception naming the file.\n- Elements in places the DTD doesn't allow are rejected.\n- Required children are enforced: changeSpeed needs speed and term, changeDirection needs direction and term, accel needs term, repeat needs times plus an action or actionRef.\n- Invalid, misspelled or misplaced type attributes are rejected. A direction with a bad type is no longer silently treated as aim.\n- actionRef, bulletRef and fireRef must have a label.\n- BulletPattern.MyValidationEventHandler has been removed.\n\nFixed:\n- Bullets that fire themselves (recursive bulletRef) no longer crash with a stack overflow.\n- Circular actionRef chains are reported as an error instead of overflowing the stack.\n- A fire node with no bullet or bulletRef reports which node is broken, instead of throwing a NullReferenceException.\n- speed, horizontal and vertical now default to absolute, as the spec says.\n\nFull release notes: https://github.com/dmanning23/BulletMLLib/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
